InfoTransfer
Original application code: Apache-2.0.

Inspired by Handy by CJ Pais (MIT), https://github.com/cjpais/Handy.
The settings layout, navigation and motion were modeled on Handy's design.
No Handy code, icons or artwork are included.

Lucide 0.542.0 icons: ISC, with Feather portions under MIT.
The complete upstream license is preserved in assets/icons/LICENSE.

Speech asset provenance and transformations: resources/SPEECH-NOTICES.txt.
Pinned downloaded artifacts: resources/*manifest.json.
The application uses sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0), ONNX Runtime (MIT),
GPUI (Apache-2.0), and onnx-protobuf (MPL-2.0).
Exact crate revisions are pinned in Cargo.lock. Full binary dependency
notices and distribution compatibility remain a public-release gate.

Offline new-word pronunciation uses a separate eSpeak NG 1.52.0 executable
(GPL-3.0-or-later), revision 4870adfa25b1a32b4361592f1be8a40337c58d6c.
Its full license, exact corresponding source and build instructions are
included in the bundle's Resources/phonemizer directory. It produces
phonemes only; the selected neural model produces the audio.
